  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EnDev Demand-Side Subsidies Component: Baseline Study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With funding from the Directorate-General for International Cooperation (DGIS) of the Netherlands Ministry of Foreign Affairs, EnDev seeks to contribute to the global body of knowledge on demand-side subsidies (DSS) by piloting innovative mechanisms and facilitating access to energy. The pilots focus on DSS schemes for low-income and/or displaced populations who are currently unable to access commercial off-grid solar and cooking markets. The component operates in four countries in Sub-Saharan Africa: Liberia, Malawi, Niger, and Uganda. This baseline study was conducted as part of the DSS component.The objective of the study was to determine the situation in relation to energy access and socio-economics amongst the target beneficiaries in the four pilot countries (Liberia, Niger, Malawi and Uganda), using quantitative and qualitative data to establish the baseline for measuring the performance of the pilots, as well as to set the basis for iterative learning.The baseline study focussed on one specific target group: households that face an affordability gap to access sustainable energy, such as very poor households, refugees, internally displaced persons (IDPs) and other marginalised groups.</narrative>
  </description>
